		<item>
			<title>Madonna To Team Up With Lourdes For New Music?</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/7-madonna-to-team-up-with-lourdes-for-new-music?.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/7-madonna-to-team-up-with-lourdes-for-new-music?.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>The 52-year-old recruited Lourdes for It's So Cool, a track which could also feature on Madge's next album, or on the soundtrack to her upcoming film, W.E., which she is directing. Find out more, click on Read More.</p>
</div><div class="K2FeedFullText">
<p>A source told The Sun that Lourdes's foray into music is no gimmick, as she has a great voice and plenty of character.</p>
<p>The insider added: 'Madonna hopes Lourdes will step into her shoes and become one of the biggest female artists in the world.</p>
<p>'She is the perfect mentor for her daughter and is keen to assist her first steps into the music industry.'</p>
<p> </p>
<p>The song in question was actually recorded acoustically by the pair back in 2003, but a subsequent release had Lourdes's vocals removed.</p>
<p>However, the single is not the only current collaboration between mother and daughter, with Madonna and Lourdes also working together on the Material Girl fashion line.</p>
<p>Kelly Osbourne was named as the new face of the clothing label back in January, replacing Gossip Girl star Taylor Momsen.</p>
<p>Lourdes was supposedly the driving force behind the switch, with reports suggesting that the youngster 'idolises' Kelly.</p></div><div class="K2FeedTags"><ul><li>Music</li><li>Lola</li><li>W.E.</li><ul></div>]]></description>
			<category>Music</category>
			<pubDate>Wed, 11 May 2011 15:38:22 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Madonna's Fire-Damaged Childhood Home On Sale</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/6-madonnas-fire-damaged-childhood-home-on-sale.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/6-madonnas-fire-damaged-childhood-home-on-sale.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p><a href="http://www.contactmusic.com" target="_blank" title="contact music">contactmusic.com</a></p>
<p>Madonna's childhood home in Michigan has been placed on the market for a paltry $48,600 (£30,375).</p>
<p>The pop superstar spent her youth in the four-bedroom Rochester Hills house with her parents and six brothers and sisters before relocating to New York in her search for fame and fortune.</p>
<p>Her family reportedly sold the property in 2001 for $270,000 (£168,750), but the home was ravaged in a fire in 2008 and has not been restored since, according to real estate blog Curbed.com.</p></div><div class="K2FeedTags"><ul><li>Rochester Hills</li><li>Detroit</li><ul></div>]]></description>
